Sītā lovingly angered answers devoted Rāma --- Sītā declares kin enjoy own merits while wife alone shares husband's fate --- Sītā claims forest exile order as her own, vows to walk ahead treading Kuśa thorns --- Sītā sets jealousy aside and begs stainless trust, prefers husband's foot-shade above palaces and sky-chariots --- Sītā cites parents teaching and vows forest joy like father's house --- Sītā vows celibate service sporting in honey-scented woods, claims Rāma can protect even others --- Sītā longs fearless for rivers hills lakes woods lotus ponds with Rāma --- Sītā scorns heaven itself without Rāma and begs to be led or face death
